 Network Traffic Analysis with tcpdump
 Overview

This project demonstrates the analysis of network traffic using tcpdump to investigate a cybersecurity incident involving DNS resolution failure.

The objective was to identify which network protocol was affected and determine the possible cause of the issue.

 Scenario

Users reported that they were unable to access a website and received the error:

“Destination port unreachable”

The issue was reproduced and analyzed using tcpdump.

 Analysis

During the packet capture, the following was observed:

DNS requests were sent using UDP (port 53)
The server responded with ICMP error messages
Error message: “destination unreachable – port 53”

This indicates that the DNS service was not accessible.

 Key Findings
UDP is used for DNS communication
Port 53 is required for DNS resolution
ICMP reported that the destination port was unreachable
DNS resolution failed, preventing access to the website
 Possible Causes
DNS server unavailable
Firewall blocking port 53
Misconfiguration of DNS service
Potential DDoS attack (requires further investigation)
🛠️ Tools Used
tcpdump
Basic networking protocols (DNS, UDP, ICMP)
